<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Git on brainboxemb</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/git/</link><description>Recent content in Git on brainboxemb</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/git/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Useful Git Commands</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/git/useful-commands/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/git/useful-commands/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Practical commands for everyday Git work. Steps that depend on GitHub are explicitly labelled.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="clone-a-repository"&gt;Clone a repository&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open the terminal in Visual Studio Code and choose the parent directory before cloning:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;cd C:\projects
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git clone &amp;lt;repository-url&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GitHub example:&lt;/strong&gt; include the account name in the HTTPS URL when you work with multiple GitHub accounts:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git clone https&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;//username@github.com/username/repository-name.git
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Open the checkout in Visual Studio Code and inspect the configured remote:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;cd repository-name
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;code .
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;git remote -v
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The username in the URL identifies the intended account; authentication is handled separately, normally by Git Credential Manager.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>